// ae help: what a configuration script got wrong, and how to fix it.
//
// This file does not compile, on purpose. A configuration written in
// Aether is code, and someone who knows YAML or HCL writes `port: 9990`
// or `host = "127.0.0.1"` in it. The compiler says only that it expected
// a statement. `ae help file.ae` reads the same file and says what was
// meant: each finding has the line, what it looks like, the suggestion
// (`port(9990)`), and whether `--fix` can apply it. `ae help --fix`
// applies the safe ones after showing the diff, and `--json` gives the
// findings to a tool. The YAML and HCL lines stop the parse, so the
// misspelt setter (`superuser_tokn`) is found once they are fixed: then it
// gets a "did you mean", from the names the imported module exports.
// help.sh shows both runs, the second in a copy with the two rewrites
// made. It all runs on the machine: no network. fixed.ae is the result.
//
// Run: sh examples/06-tooling/05-ae-help/help.sh
// See: docs/cic-help.md

import my_lib

main() {
    my_lib.serve() {
        port: 9990
        host = "127.0.0.1"
        superuser_tokn("admin-1234")
        repo("alpha", "/data/alpha")
    }
}

// Output:
//
// ae help, 2 findings for examples/06-tooling/05-ae-help/broken.ae
//
// [1] YAML-style colon at examples/06-tooling/05-ae-help/broken.ae:23:9
//     port on line 23 looks like YAML; Aether setters use call form
//       23 |         port: 9990
//          |         ^
//     help: Did you mean: port(9990)?
//     (safe to auto-apply with --fix)
//     see:  docs/closures-and-builder-dsl.md
//
// [2] HCL-style equals at examples/06-tooling/05-ae-help/broken.ae:24:9
//     host on line 24 looks like HCL; Aether setters use call form
//       24 |         host = "127.0.0.1"
//          |         ^
//     help: Did you mean: host("127.0.0.1")?
//     (safe to auto-apply with --fix)
//     see:  docs/closures-and-builder-dsl.md
//
// --- with those two rewrites made:
//
// ae help, 1 finding for broken.ae
//
// [1] undefined function at broken.ae:25:9
//     Undefined function 'superuser_tokn'
//       25 |         superuser_tokn("admin-1234")
//          |         ^
//     help: Did you mean: superuser_token (in my_lib)?
//     (safe to auto-apply with --fix)
//     see:  docs/module-system-design.md (Selective import / exports)
